From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alejandro Corbellini <acorbellini@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 03 Mar 2026 10:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: rk817-battery: force OCV recalibration on
 boot

When u-boot initializes the fuel gauge (is_initialized=true), the
kernel driver blindly trusts the saved dsoc without any OCV
validation. If u-boot's calibration is wrong, the reported capacity
can be stuck far from reality (e.g. 55% at 4.3V) for hours until
the smooth algorithm slowly corrects it.

Fix this by performing an OCV voltage check even when u-boot has
initialized the gauge. If the OCV-based SOC differs from the saved
SOC by more than max_soc_offset (default 60%), override it. This
ensures the battery percentage is reasonably accurate from boot
rather than taking hours to converge.

Guard against bogus OCV readings (e.g. 17mV when the ADC register
has not yet been populated) by requiring the OCV voltage to be at
least 2500mV before using it. A connected Li-ion cell can never be
below ~2.5V in practice; if the reading is lower, skip recalibration
and trust u-boot's value.

Note: vol_to_soc() returns 0-100 but dsoc is stored as percentage
times 1000 (0-100000), so scale appropriately when comparing and
assigning.

Signed-off-by: Alejandro Corbellini <acorbellini@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/rk817_battery.c | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/rk817_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/rk817_battery.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/rk817_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/rk817_battery.c
@@ -1638,7 +1638,35 @@
 		goto finish;
 	} else if (battery->is_initialized) {
 		/* uboot initialized */
-		BAT_INFO("initialized yet..\n");
+		BAT_INFO("uboot initialized: pre_soc=%d, pre_cap=%d\n",
+			 pre_soc, pre_cap);
+		/* Validate u-boot's SOC against OCV measurement.
+		 * vol_to_soc returns 0-100, but dsoc is 0-100000
+		 * (percentage * 1000), so scale for comparison.
+		 */
+		ocv_vol = rk817_bat_get_ocv_voltage(battery);
+		/* Sanity-check: a connected Li-ion cell is never below
+		 * ~2.5 V. If the OCV register returns less than 2500 mV
+		 * the ADC was not ready yet -- skip recalibration. */
+		if (ocv_vol < 2500) {
+			BAT_INFO("OCV reading too low (%d mV), "
+				 "skipping recalibration\n", ocv_vol);
+			goto finish;
+		}
+		ocv_soc = rk817_bat_vol_to_soc(battery, ocv_vol);
+		ocv_cap = rk817_bat_vol_to_cap(battery, ocv_vol);
+		if (abs(ocv_soc * 1000 - pre_soc) >=
+		    battery->pdata->max_soc_offset * 1000) {
+			BAT_INFO("uboot SOC wrong, OCV recalib: "
+				 "dsoc %d -> %d (ocv_vol=%d)\n",
+				 pre_soc / 1000, ocv_soc, ocv_vol);
+			pre_soc = ocv_soc * 1000;
+			pre_cap = ocv_cap;
+			rk817_bat_init_coulomb_cap(battery, ocv_cap);
+		} else {
+			BAT_INFO("uboot SOC ok (ocv_soc=%d, ocv_vol=%d)\n",
+				 ocv_soc, ocv_vol);
+		}
 		goto finish;
 	} else if (battery->is_ocv_calib) {
 		/* not initialized and poweroff_cnt above 30 min */
--
